            <ArticleTitle>The Use of Particulated Juvenile Allograft Cartilage in Foot and Ankle Surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11-18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0891-8422(17)30084-8</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cpm.2017.08.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Particulated juvenile allograft cartilage (PJAC) has significant promise and is currently supported by several studies. Potential benefits of this new technique include single-stage procedure, simplicity in the surgical technique, implantation of juvenile tissue, and a lack of donor site morbidity. This article discusses the imaging, surgical options, and postoperative management of PJAC.</AbstractText>
